    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <!-- Use this file to provide workspace-specific custom instructions to Copilot -->
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: # Shortify Project Instructions
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: This is a PHP-based URL shortener project using MariaDB and NGINX. (Regeln 1-9, Key components wie im Original.)
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 1. Follow PSR-4 autoloading standards for PHP classes
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 2. Use prepared statements for all database queries to prevent SQL injection
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 3. Implement proper input validation for URLs
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 4. Maintain URL visit tracking functionality
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 5. Keep the Docker configuration synchronized across Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, and nginx.conf
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 6. Follow RESTful principles for API endpoints
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 7. Maintain responsive design in the frontend HTML/CSS
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 8. Ensure proper error handling and logging
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 9. Keep security best practices in mind, especially for URL validation and database access
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: Key components: URLShortener class, urls table mit visit tracking, vanilla JS frontend, Docker PHP-FPM+NGINX+MariaDB.
